#!RuleTest
#test FDA-CT2003 expect=noViolation domain=LB
#note "Every populated LBTESTCD maps to the same CDISC-CT concept id as its paired LBTEST decode (ALB/Albumin = C64431, BILI/Bilirubin = C64433), so the one-to-one relationship holds and the rule stays silent. The empty row proves the 'not empty(value())' guard: an unpopulated code is not a finding."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#library codelist-codes LB LBTESTCD ALB=C64431 BILI=C64433
#library codelist-codes LB LBTEST Albumin=C64431 Bilirubin=C64433
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset LB label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBTEST   type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Name"
---
S1 | LB | 001 | ALB | Albumin
S1 | LB | 002 | BILI | Bilirubin
S1 | LB | 003 |  |
